1
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:05,040
How'd someone get your credit card number?

2
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:07,670
I have no idea. Look how much they spent!

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:08,970
Monica, Calm down.

4
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:11,590
You only have to pay for the stuff you bought.

5
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:14,510
Still, it's just such reckless spending.

6
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,590
When somebody steals your credit card...

7
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:19,810
...they've kind of already thrown caution to the wind.

8
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:28,060
Wow, what a geek. They spent $69.95 on a Wonder Mop.

9
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:31,150
That's me.

10
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,110
Oh! Oh, the yuck.

11
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:37,780
He's doing it again!

12
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:40,240
Marcel, stop humping the lamp!

13
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:42,790
Stop humping! Now, Marcel, come back!

14
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:44,120
Come here, Marcel!

15
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:46,500
Oh, no, no! Not in my room! I'll get him.

16
00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:49,670
You've got to do something about the humping.

17
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,090
What? It's just a phase.

18
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:55,090
Well, that's what we said about Joey.

19
00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:00,680
Hey, would you all relax? It's not that big a deal.

20
00:01:00,890 --> 00:01:03,220
Marcel, stop it! Marcel! Bad monkey!

21
00:01:03,390 --> 00:01:04,680
What?

22
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:09,250
Let's just say my Curious George doll is no longer curious.

23
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:03,700
Ugh, Monica, you are not still going over that thing.

24
00:02:03,870 --> 00:02:06,700
This woman's living my life.

25
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:10,830
She's living my life, and she's doing it better than me.

26
00:02:11,210 --> 00:02:13,250
Look at this. Look.

27
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:16,090
She buys tickets to plays I want to see.

28
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:19,590
She shops at stores that I'm intimidated by the salespeople.

29
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:22,340
She spent $300 on art supplies.

30
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:23,890
You're not an artist.

31
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:27,060
Yeah, well, I might be if I had the supplies.

32
00:02:27,810 --> 00:02:32,190
I mean, I could do all this stuff. Only I don't.

33
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:35,110
Oh, Monica, come on. You do cool things.

34
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,440
Oh, really? Let's compare, shall we?

35
00:02:37,610 --> 00:02:41,110
Oh, it's so late for "shall we?"

36
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:44,120
Do I go horseback riding in the park, hmm?

37
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:46,330
Do I take classes at The New School?

38
00:02:46,490 --> 00:02:48,500
No.

39
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,370
This is so unfair.

40
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:53,960
She's got everything I want, and she doesn't have my mother.

41
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:04,550
How about Joey Paponi?

42
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:07,000
No, still too ethnic.

43
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,930
My agent thinks I should have a name that's more neutral.

44
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:10,930
Joey Switzerland?

45
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:20,190
Plus I think it should be Joe. Joey makes me sound like I'm...

46
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,610
...this big.

47
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:22,990
Which I'm not!

48
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:28,870
Joe, Joe, Joe... Stalin?

49
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:32,290
Stalin.

50
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:35,710
Do I know that name? That sounds familiar.

51
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:39,420
Well, it does not ring a bell with me.

52
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:42,800
Joe Stalin.

53
00:03:45,010 --> 00:03:46,850
You know, that's pretty good.

54
00:03:47,510 --> 00:03:49,560
You might want to try Joseph.

55
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:58,520
Joseph Stalin!

56
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:01,320
I think you'd remember that!

57
00:04:03,070 --> 00:04:05,700
Bye Bye Birdie, starring Joseph Stalin.

58
00:04:05,910 --> 00:04:09,580
Joseph Stalin is the Fiddler on the Roof.

59
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,090
Hey.

60
00:04:19,250 --> 00:04:20,590
Hi.

61
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:24,840
Hi. Uh, yes, this is Monica Geller.

62
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:29,950
Um, I'm taking classes with you, and I was wondering what they were.

63
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:33,140
What are you doing?

64
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:34,640
All right, great.

65
00:04:34,850 --> 00:04:36,810
Great. Thanks a lot.

66
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:38,810
I'm going to tap class.

67
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:42,230
So you can dance with the woman that stole your card?

68
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,820
She's got my life. I want to see who she is.

69
00:04:44,990 --> 00:04:47,960
Go to the post office! I'm sure her picture's up!

70
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:51,240
Honey, you're kind of losing it here.

71
00:04:51,410 --> 00:04:54,250
This is really becoming a weird obsession.

72
00:04:54,410 --> 00:04:56,250
This is madness, I tell you.

73
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:59,240
For the love of God, Monica, don't do it!

74
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:04,130
Thank you.

75
00:05:11,430 --> 00:05:13,100
What do you think?

76
00:05:13,270 --> 00:05:15,270
Lots of things.

77
00:05:16,230 --> 00:05:18,100
Which one do you think she is?

78
00:05:18,310 --> 00:05:19,940
May I help you?

79
00:05:18,310 --> 00:05:19,940
Oh, no, thanks.

80
00:05:20,110 --> 00:05:21,860
We're just here to observe.

81
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:25,900
You don't observe a dance class. You dance a dance class!

82
00:05:26,070 --> 00:05:27,400
Spare shoes are over there.

83
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:32,030
What does she mean?

84
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,080
I think she means, "You dance...

85
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:35,910
...a dance class!"

86
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,910
Come on, come on, come on!

87
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,670
Really?

88
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:42,790
Hey, do you see anybody you think could be me?

89
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:47,590
People, last time there were yogurt containers lying around after class.

90
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:49,990
Let's not have that happen again!

91
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:52,140
She could be you.

92
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:58,060
Let's get started.

93
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:02,690
Five, six. Five, six, seven, eight.

94
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,240
Okay, I'm not getting this!

95
00:06:09,450 --> 00:06:12,530
I'm totally getting it!

96
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:20,420
Do you ever just feel like you're so unbelievably uncoordinated?

97
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:30,930
What? You just click when they click.

98
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:34,810
All right. Now everyone grab a partner.

99
00:06:34,970 --> 00:06:36,470
Oh! Oh.

100
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:41,600
All right. And my dead mother said you are it! I'm with Rachel.

101
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:44,730
Great, it's gym class all over again.

102
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,400
Aww.

103
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:50,780
That's all right. You can come up to the front and dance with me.

104
00:06:51,450 --> 00:06:54,990
Why don't I just take off my clothes and have a nightmare?

105
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:04,960
It's okay, it's okay! I'm here, I'm here. I'm so sorry I'm late.

106
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:06,380
Okay, here I am.

107
00:07:06,550 --> 00:07:09,050
So who's the new tense girl?

108
00:07:09,550 --> 00:07:10,760
She's your partner.

109
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:12,680
Hi, I'm Monica.

110
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:15,390
Oh, ha.

111
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,680
Monica.

112
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:19,850
Hi, I'm Mon...

113
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,060
Nana.

114
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:23,560
Monana?

115
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:23,560
Yeah.

116
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:25,610
It's Dutch.

117
00:07:25,770 --> 00:07:28,360
You're kidding. I spent three years in Amsterdam.

118
00:07:31,990 --> 00:07:35,160
Um, Pennsylvania Dutch.

119
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:37,620
And we're dancing!

120
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:40,540
Five, six, seven, eight.

121
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:48,920
Hi.

122
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:52,340
Hey.

123
00:07:52,510 --> 00:07:55,760
Where have You been?

124
00:07:52,510 --> 00:07:55,760
I just got back from the vet.

125
00:07:55,970 --> 00:07:59,600
She's not gonna make you wear a big plastic cone, is she?

126
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:05,650
She says Marcel's humping thing is not a phase.

127
00:08:05,810 --> 00:08:09,070
Apparently, he's reached sexual maturity.

128
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:12,150
Hey, he beat you!

129
00:08:15,910 --> 00:08:20,910
She says, as time goes on, he'll start getting aggressive and violent.

130
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,580
What does this mean?

131
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,920
I have to give him up.

132
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:46,650
I can't believe it, Rose. This sucks!

133
00:08:46,810 --> 00:08:50,320
You just got him. How could he be an adult already?

134
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:53,780
I know, I know. One day he's this little thing...

135
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:56,450
...and before you know it, he's this little thing...

136
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:59,240
...I can't get off my leg.

137
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:02,450
Isn't there any way you can keep him?

138
00:09:02,620 --> 00:09:03,660
No. No.

139
00:09:03,830 --> 00:09:07,670
The vet said that unless he's in a place where he has regular access...

140
00:09:07,830 --> 00:09:12,090
...to some monkey loving...

141
00:09:13,170 --> 00:09:15,130
...he's just gonna get vicious.

142
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:18,780
I just gotta get him into a zoo.

143
00:09:20,050 --> 00:09:23,450
How do you get a monkey into a zoo?

144
00:09:20,050 --> 00:09:23,450
I know that one!

145
00:09:27,350 --> 00:09:30,270
No, that's popes into a Volkswagen.

146
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:36,240
We're applying to a lot of them. Our first choice would be a state zoo.

147
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:39,030
You know, like, uh, San Diego.

148
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:41,370
Right?

149
00:09:41,530 --> 00:09:45,870
But that may just be a pipe dream because he's out-of-state.

150
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:52,500
My vet knows someone at Miami, so that's a possibility.

151
00:09:52,670 --> 00:09:56,970
But that's two blocks from the beach. It's a total party zoo.

152
00:10:00,930 --> 00:10:02,010
Hey.

153
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:03,970
We found the girl!

154
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:05,770
Did You call the cops?

155
00:10:05,930 --> 00:10:07,520
Nope. We took her to lunch.

156
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:10,400
Ah. Your own brand of vigilante justice.

157
00:10:12,190 --> 00:10:14,730
Are you insane? This woman stole from you!

158
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:17,490
She stole! She's a stealer!

159
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:21,960
After you're with this woman for 10 minutes, you forget all that.

160
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:25,870
I mean, she's this astounding person...

161
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:28,250
...with this amazing spirit!

162
00:10:28,410 --> 00:10:31,540
Yeah, which she probably stole from some cheerleader!

163
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:36,210
Take off their hats.

164
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:36,210
Popes in a Volkswagen!

165
00:10:36,380 --> 00:10:37,670
Mm-hm.

166
00:10:39,590 --> 00:10:41,680
I love that joke.

167
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:50,190
No way! No way did you do this!

168
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:50,190
Monana was very brave.

169
00:10:50,730 --> 00:10:51,940
It was so wild.

170
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:55,070
We told them we were the Gunnersons in room 615...

171
00:10:55,230 --> 00:10:59,110
...only to find out the Boston Celtics had the entire sixth floor!

172
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:02,780
So when they caught on to the fact that we're short and have breasts...

173
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:06,990
They threw us out. I was thrown out of a hotel! Me!

174
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:09,160
Go, Monana!

175
00:11:11,290 --> 00:11:14,960
Well, you ladies are not the only ones living the dream.

176
00:11:15,130 --> 00:11:20,010
I get to go pour coffee for people I don't know. Don't wait up.

177
00:11:21,430 --> 00:11:23,340
Oh, by the way...

178
00:11:23,510 --> 00:11:26,810
...tomorrow we're auditioning for a Broadway show.

179
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,310
Excuse me?

180
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,180
There's an open call for Cats.

181
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:34,190
I'm thinking we go down there, sing "Memories"...

182
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:37,940
...and make complete fools of ourselves. What do you say?

183
00:11:38,190 --> 00:11:40,490
No, no, no.

184
00:11:40,650 --> 00:11:43,320
Remember who you're dealing with here. Ha.

185
00:11:43,490 --> 00:11:46,660
I'm not like you. I can't even stand in front of a tap class.

186
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:49,530
That's because of your Amish background.

187
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:53,920
What?

188
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:53,920
Well, you're Pennsylvania Dutch, right?

189
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:55,170
Right.

190
00:11:55,330 --> 00:11:58,840
Till I bought a blow dryer. Then I was shunned.

191
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:02,090
I was just like you.

192
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:06,220
And then one day, I saw a movie that changed my life.

193
00:12:06,850 --> 00:12:09,310
Did You ever see Dead Poets Society?

194
00:12:09,470 --> 00:12:13,140
I thought that movie was so incredibly...

195
00:12:13,310 --> 00:12:14,750
...boring!

196
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:17,060
I mean, that thing at the end where the kid...

197
00:12:17,230 --> 00:12:19,820
...kills himself because he can't be in the play?

198
00:12:20,650 --> 00:12:21,990
What was that?

199
00:12:22,150 --> 00:12:27,380
It's like, "Kid, wait a year. Leave home, do some community theater!"

200
00:12:28,950 --> 00:12:30,790
I walked out of there, and I thought:

201
00:12:30,950 --> 00:12:35,370
Now, that's two hours of my life that I'm never getting back!

202
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:39,250
And that scared me more than all the other crap I was afraid to do.

203
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,090
Wow.

204
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:44,070
Then I would definitely not recommend Mrs. Doubtfire.

205
00:12:51,390 --> 00:12:53,520
Oh, God.

206
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:57,190
We didn't get into Scranton.

207
00:12:58,860 --> 00:13:01,940
That was our safety zoo.

208
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:05,820
They take, like, dogs and cows.

209
00:13:07,990 --> 00:13:09,240
See?

210
00:13:09,410 --> 00:13:12,870
I don't know who this is harder on, me or him.

211
00:13:13,750 --> 00:13:16,620
I'd say that chair's taking the brunt of it.

212
00:13:18,670 --> 00:13:20,590
Marcel. Marcel.

213
00:13:20,750 --> 00:13:22,050
Marcel, no.

214
00:13:23,630 --> 00:13:25,260
Good boy!

215
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:27,510
See? How can nobody want him?

216
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:29,590
Somebody will.

217
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:35,970
You know there already is a Joseph Stalin?

218
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:41,650
You're kidding!

219
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:47,850
Apparently, he was this Russian dictator who slaughtered all these people!

220
00:13:48,990 --> 00:13:52,450
You'd think you would've known that!

221
00:13:48,990 --> 00:13:52,450
You'd think I would've.

222
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:59,210
Phoebe, what do you think a good stage name for me would be?

223
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,500
Flame Boy!

224
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:11,890
Where exactly is your zoo?

225
00:14:12,050 --> 00:14:14,810
Well, it's technically not a zoo per se.

226
00:14:14,970 --> 00:14:18,430
It's, uh, more of an interactive wildlife experience.

227
00:14:18,690 --> 00:14:21,310
Let me ask you some questions about... Is it, uh, Marcel?

228
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:23,060
Yes.

229
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:25,830
Does he, uh, fight with other animals?

230
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:28,320
No, no. He's very docile.

231
00:14:28,490 --> 00:14:31,740
Hmm. Even if he were cornered?

232
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:37,250
Well, I don't know. Why?

233
00:14:37,410 --> 00:14:40,460
Um, how is he at handling small objects?

234
00:14:41,710 --> 00:14:44,340
He can hold a banana, if that's what you mean.

235
00:14:45,670 --> 00:14:48,460
What about a hammer or a small blade?

236
00:14:51,550 --> 00:14:54,930
Why would he need a blade?

237
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:58,180
If he's up against a jungle cat or an animal with horns...

238
00:14:58,350 --> 00:15:00,440
...you got to give the little guy something.

239
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:02,900
Otherwise, it's just cruel!

240
00:15:05,650 --> 00:15:08,070
He got into San Diego!

241
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,400
What?

242
00:15:09,570 --> 00:15:12,820
We were coming back from our walk, and the phone was ringing...

243
00:15:12,990 --> 00:15:14,620
He's in!

244
00:15:14,780 --> 00:15:16,620
Did you hear that, Marcel?

245
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:19,580
San Diego! San Diego! Yeah!

246
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:22,870
You're making a mistake. San Diego's well and good...

247
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:26,380
...but if you give him to me, I'll start him against a blind rabbit...

248
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:28,950
...and give you 20 percent of the gate.

249
00:15:46,770 --> 00:15:48,570
Yo-ho!

250
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,110
Where have you been?

251
00:15:51,650 --> 00:15:54,240
Monica and I just crashed an embassy party.

252
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,620
Are you drunk?

253
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:59,240
No!

254
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,370
I'm lying.

255
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:06,750
I am so drunk!

256
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:08,250
Oh, God!

257
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:11,090
Ugh. Great. You know what? You could have called.

258
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:13,170
I've been up here. I've been worried...

259
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:14,720
Monica.

260
00:16:14,890 --> 00:16:16,760
Monica?

261
00:16:19,890 --> 00:16:22,520
Water rules!

262
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:27,110
Yes. Yes, it does.

263
00:16:27,270 --> 00:16:31,530
The restaurant called. They want to know if you're showing up.

264
00:16:31,690 --> 00:16:33,240
Nope!

265
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:35,780
I'm going to the Big Apple Circus today.

266
00:16:35,950 --> 00:16:39,990
What are you doing? You're gonna lose your job. This is not you!

267
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:41,910
No, it is me!

268
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:45,290
I'm not just the person who needs to fluff the pillows...

269
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:47,750
...and pay the bills as soon as they come in!

270
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:52,670
You know, when I'm with her, I'm so much more than that!

271
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,510
I'm...

272
00:16:55,470 --> 00:16:58,300
I'm Monana!

273
00:17:03,430 --> 00:17:05,560
Ahem, hello?

274
00:17:05,730 --> 00:17:07,810
Yes, she is. Hold on a second, please.

275
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:10,820
Ahem, Monana, it's for you.

276
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:12,980
The credit card people.

277
00:17:13,610 --> 00:17:15,450
Hello?

278
00:17:17,030 --> 00:17:18,660
Yes?

279
00:17:20,120 --> 00:17:22,040
Oh, my God!

280
00:17:22,910 --> 00:17:24,410
Thanks.

281
00:17:25,410 --> 00:17:26,910
What?

282
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:29,540
They've arrested Monica.

283
00:17:40,010 --> 00:17:42,350
Hi.

284
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:44,180
How are you?

285
00:17:44,350 --> 00:17:47,020
I'm not too bad. Fortunately, blue's my color.

286
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:49,770
How did you know I was here?

287
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:53,400
Because...

288
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:55,990
...I'm Monica Geller.

289
00:17:56,860 --> 00:17:59,700
It was my credit card you were using.

290
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:02,240
That I was not expecting.

291
00:18:02,410 --> 00:18:05,040
I want you to know, I didn't turn you in.

292
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,830
Oh.

293
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,080
thanks.

294
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:12,590
You have given me so much.

295
00:18:12,750 --> 00:18:14,920
If it wasn't for you, I'd never have gotten...

296
00:18:15,090 --> 00:18:17,760
...to sing "Memories" at the Winter Garden Theater.

297
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,650
Actually, you only got to sing "Memo..."

298
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:26,390
I can't believe you're in here. What am I gonna do without you?

299
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:29,100
Who's gonna crash the embassy parties with me?

300
00:18:29,270 --> 00:18:31,520
Who's gonna take me to the Big Apple Circus?

301
00:18:32,150 --> 00:18:36,570
Monica, I started my day by peeing in front of 25 other women...

302
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:41,070
...and you're worried about who will take you to the Big Apple Circus?

303
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:45,910
Well, not worried, you know, just wondering.

304
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:48,580
There's nothing to wonder about.

305
00:18:48,750 --> 00:18:52,540
You'll go back to being who you were because that's who you are.

306
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:55,420
not necessarily.

307
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:55,420
Yes, necessarily.

308
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,120
I don't know what it is.

309
00:18:57,120 --> 00:18:58,460
Maybe it's the Amish thing.

310
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:04,600
Um, I'm not actually Amish.

311
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:07,810
Really? Then why are you like that?

312
00:19:23,450 --> 00:19:25,730
You by the door, in or out?

313
00:19:26,990 --> 00:19:28,330
In!

314
00:19:33,790 --> 00:19:35,840
You in the back, you're getting it wrong!

315
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,840
At least I'm doing it!

316
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:56,480
This is the final boarding call for Flight 67 to San Diego...

317
00:19:56,650 --> 00:19:58,980
...boarding at Gate 42A.

318
00:19:59,150 --> 00:20:01,530
Okay, goodbye, little monkey guy.

319
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:04,990
I wrote You This poem.

320
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:07,870
Okay, but don't eat it till you get on the plane.

321
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,910
thank You, Aunt Phoebe.

322
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:16,380
Okay, bye, champ.

323
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:19,420
There's gonna be a lot of babes in San Diego...

324
00:20:19,590 --> 00:20:23,130
...but remember, there's also a lot to learn.

325
00:20:28,930 --> 00:20:32,560
I don't know what to say, Ross. Uh, it's a monkey.

326
00:20:32,730 --> 00:20:36,020
Just say what you feel, Joey.

327
00:20:37,230 --> 00:20:38,810
Marcel, I'm hungry.

328
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:40,860
That was good.

329
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:46,450
Marcel, This is for you.

330
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:50,490
It's, uh, just, you know, something to, um...

331
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,370
...do on the plane.

332
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:59,210
If you don't mind, I'd like a moment, just me and him.

333
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:02,380
Of course. Absolutely.

334
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:05,260
Oh.

335
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:09,970
Marcel, come here. Come here.

336
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:11,850
Come here.

337
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:13,640
Well, buddy...

338
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:17,060
...this is it.

339
00:21:17,230 --> 00:21:20,360
There's just a couple of things I wanted to say.

340
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:24,360
I'm really gonna miss you.

341
00:21:24,530 --> 00:21:27,450
You know? And I'm never gonna forget about you.

342
00:21:27,610 --> 00:21:32,490
You've been more than just a pet to me.

343
00:21:32,790 --> 00:21:34,290
You've been more like a...

344
00:21:34,450 --> 00:21:36,580
Okay. Marcel, would you...?

345
00:21:37,370 --> 00:21:39,630
Marcel, would you leave my leg alone?

346
00:21:39,790 --> 00:21:43,420
Would you just stop humping me for two seconds? Marc... Would you...?

347
00:21:43,590 --> 00:21:47,430
Okay, would you just take him away? Just take him.

348
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:13,160
O! That I were a glove upon that hand...

349
00:22:13,330 --> 00:22:17,040
...that I might touch thy cheek.

350
00:22:17,210 --> 00:22:19,870
That's fine. Thank you.

351
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:21,830
Next.

352
00:22:25,550 --> 00:22:28,340
Hi. Uh, I'll be reading for the role of Mercutio.

353
00:22:28,510 --> 00:22:31,470
Name?

354
00:22:28,510 --> 00:22:31,470
Holden McGroin.

